WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.321
Best known for his role as sadistic boy-king
Joffrey Baratheon in Game of Thrones, Irish

00:00:06.321 --> 00:00:11.700
actor Jack Gleeson seemed poised for big things
but for a while, he was pretty much nowhere

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.360
to be found.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.140
So exactly what happened to him?

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.880
Here's an important thing to know: Gleeson
really isn't interested in living an actor's

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.380
lifestyle.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.080
In an interview with the Irish Independent,
Gleeson said:

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.840
"When I started doing Game of Thrones, perhaps
the reality was made too real for me.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.289
The lifestyle that comes with being an actor
in a successful TV show isn't something I

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.440
gravitate towards."

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.740
In fact, he only started acting because it
was just something for him to do.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.080
Gleeson started taking acting classes with
his two older sisters at his local community

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.660
center because there wasn't much else available.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.660
He told Vulture:

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.120
"It was nearby [...] I did it because it looked
fun.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.200
If the community center hosted karate classes
instead, I might be a karate person, but for

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.260
some reason they happened to have acting classes,
so I went to them."

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.520
Perhaps the main reason Gleeson didn't much
like playing Joffrey was that he just didn't

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:01.900
enjoy working on set.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:02.960
“You can’t…”

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:09.400
Specifically, Gleeson isn't intrigued by the
faker aspects of filming an effects-heavy

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.760
show like Game of Thrones.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.520
He explained to Vulture:

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.560
"When you go on to a set, you realize the
very visceral reality that you see on the

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:23.300
TV show is a product of a huge amount of processing
and editing and storytelling that isn’t

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.180
present on the day of filming.”

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.590
Worse yet, Gleeson found actually doing his
job to be almost entirely unfulfilling — and

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.480
incredibly boring.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.240
He said:

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.490
"You go and put your makeup on, put your costume
on, wait in your caravan-trailer thing for

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:44.840
an hour and then you go the set, and you film
for three minutes and then they change around

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.480
the lights, and the camera angle and you wait
for an hour, and then you film for another

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.120
three minutes.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.720
It's a very boring, tedious process."

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.360
Gleeson was so not into it, in fact, that
his favorite moment of filming actually came

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:02.940
when he played dead during Joffrey's funeral,
simply because he got to sleep all day.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.500
He joked:

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.840
"That was a fun experience."

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.460
Gleeson doesn't have any special attachments
to the show which made him famous, either.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.859
In fact, he couldn't care less about the show
or the novels on which it was based of which

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:18.849
he only made it through one, before realizing
he didn't have the attention span required

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:19.600
to continue.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.320
And as for the T.V. series, Gleeson explained:

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.700
"There's too much to catch up on.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.380
I've not a clue what's going on.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:30.219
In my mind, all these characters are still
alive and everyone's in this place and those

00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:34.909
people are in that place and they have these
motivations, and now everything's screwed

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:37.160
around so much that it's a completely different
show.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.260
I've no idea."

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.240
Gleeson's not bluffing either.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.600
He really doesn't have a clue since he only
ever read his own scenes from the script.

00:02:44.609 --> 00:02:45.609
He told Vulture:

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:46.380
"I'm just selfish.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.540
Maybe I should get into it.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.600
I hear it's good."

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:54.300
While his stint on Game of Thrones might have
landed Gleeson with a whole heap of fame and

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.900
money, he has admitted that he doesn't really
care for either.

00:02:57.129 --> 00:03:02.240
The former actor claims to live as normal
a life as possible, residing alone in a London

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.500
flat he describes as nothing out of the ordinary.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.280
Even today, he'd rather keep it simple and
go about his business than focus on remaining

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:09.860
a celebrity.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.020
Gleeson explains:

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.540
"It's maybe the status thing that I find uncomfortable.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:18.189
People can be wealthy and not be mean, but
this status thing [...] some people when they

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:21.280
become famous, they feel better, they feel
more worthy.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.420
That's what makes me feel really uncomfortable.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.300
I try to eschew that as much as possible."

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:32.980
Still, Gleeson is always happy to snap some
photos with fans, retweet jokes about Joffrey,

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.380
and attend the occasional convention.

00:03:35.049 --> 00:03:39.699
And as for money, well, it's no secret that
Game of Thrones actors make bank Gleeson included

00:03:39.699 --> 00:03:41.799
but the young Irishman doesn't really care.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.020
For Gleeson, money truly isn't everything.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.600
He told the Irish Independent:

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.739
"I'm happy to sacrifice a big paycheck for
my happiness, if that's not too corny a thing

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.240
to say.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:56.020
It's probably more naive than mature to say
that, maybe, but that's how I feel."

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.500
Even though Gleeson seems pretty disinterested
with on-screen acting, you'll still be seeing

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.000
him on TV in the near future just maybe not
where you might expect.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.140
Coming off his off-Broadway puppet show Bears
in Space, Gleeson saw himself fitting in nicely

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.980
on another popular, children-themed, but adult-oriented,
television program, explaining to Vulture:

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.920
"My dream is getting into some Adult Swim–style
[thing] — short little bursts of wackiness,

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.160
maybe a multimedia thing with puppets and
animation and live action."

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.900
In 2016, he also told the Herald Sun:

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.300
"I wanted to be a big famous successful actor.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.940
I suppose something just changed.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.580
I still love acting, and I see myself acting
in the future, but that kind of spark is not

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.080
there anymore."

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.300
But it looks like that spark has returned.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:47.900
In early 2020, Gleeson came out of retirement
to be cast in Out of Her Mind, a BBC Two series

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:53.300
by comedian Sara Pascoe that promises to include
a cast of bizarre characters, as well as those

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.820
unusual animations that Gleeson was looking
to be a part of.

